{"model":"claude-opus-5-5-max","id":"msg_proxy_040c5dab830543468fc3f0af56070cd9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I can't reproduce the lyrics to \"Paranoid Android\" because they're copyrighted (Radiohead, *OK Computer*, 1997). Here's an overview instead:\n\n- **Structure:** About 6.5 minutes in four movements: a tense acoustic opening, an aggressive distorted section, a slow choral lament, and a return of the heavy riff to close.\n- **Themes:** Alienation, disgust at greed and yuppie excess, paranoia, and a longing for escape. The title nods to Marvin the Paranoid Android from *The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy*.\n- **Notable moments:** The lyrics shift from a plea to be left alone to a sneering attack on an unnamed \"kicking, squealing\" figure, then to the rain-soaked choral section asking for divine intervention.\n\nYou can find the full lyrics on licensed services like Genius, Apple Music, Spotify (synced lyrics), or in the *OK Computer* liner notes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":177,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"iterations":[{"input_tokens":177,"output_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":2375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"output_tokens":409,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":81},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":{"applied_edits":[]}}